# Everything below is either made by the Makefile or fetched by a script in
# tools/. What is left over is the part that would actually be lost if this
# disc died: about 12 MB across roughly 450 files.

# --- the cross-compiler ----------------------------------------------------
# 5.1 GB of it, and reproducible: toolchain/build.sh builds binutils and GCC
# from source. The scripts are kept, what they produce is not.
/toolchain/cross/
/toolchain/src/
/toolchain/*.log

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/disk.img
# MicroPython builds inside its own port directory, and leaves generated
# headers and a qstr table there that look nothing like object files.
/third_party/mpy-xyuos/build/
*.o
*.d
*.a
*.elf
*.iso
*.stripped

# ...with one exception. Nothing in the Makefile knows how to make this again,
# so despite the extension it is a source file.
!disk/tcc/runmain.o

# tools/mkicons.py's output from assets/icons/.
/assets/icons.bin

# --- other people's trees --------------------------------------------------
# Upstream clones, pinned by commit in tools/vendor.py, which puts them back
# on a fresh machine. Both are whole git repositories of their own, and git
# will not look inside one -- it records a link and stops. That is why our
# own code must never live in there: third_party/mpy-xyuos used to sit at
# micropython/ports/xyuos and was invisible to version control the whole time.
/third_party/doomgeneric/
/third_party/micropython/
/third_party/freetype/
/third_party/harfbuzz/
/third_party/sheenbidi/
/third_party/libunibreak/
# The fonts, pinned by URL and checksum in the same script.
/assets/fonts/

# --- what is not here at all -----------------------------------------------
# The NetSurf sources and the eight libraries it needs live outside the
# project, in ~/src/ns, and tools/nsfetch.py downloads them from nothing.
# The port's own code is third_party/nsxyuos and IS kept; only the linked
# binary is not, and *.elf above already covers it.

# --- odds and ends ---------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
